#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# undefined

#% text
# `undefined` is the value of an expression that has none, such as `conditional_expression(a, false)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Arithmetic propagates it: a sum, product or power with `undefined` as an operand is `undefined`, `0*undefined` included.

#% item
# The numeric functions propagate it: a call of a function that numerical evaluation computes (`sin`, `exp`, `gamma`, `bessel_j`, `zeta`, ...) with `undefined` as an argument is `undefined`. A list argument is mapped over first, so only the entries that are `undefined` give `undefined`.

#% item
# Nothing else does: comparisons, `and`, `or`, `not`, `if`, lists, associations, rules, calls of other functions, held arguments and `quote` keep `undefined` as it is.

#% item
# `n(undefined)` is `undefined`. Test for it with `===`: `v === undefined`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Arithmetic and numeric functions of `undefined` are `undefined`:

#% cell
[1 + undefined, 0*undefined, undefined^2, sin(undefined), bessel_j(0, undefined)]
#% output
#= [undefined, undefined, undefined, undefined, undefined]

#% text
# A comparison stays a comparison:

#% cell
a == 1 + sin(undefined)
#% output
#= a == undefined

#% text
# A list keeps its entries:

#% cell
[1, undefined, x]
#% output
#= [1, undefined, x]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A condition that cannot hold gives `undefined`, and arithmetic with it stays `undefined`:

#% cell
conditional_expression(x^2, x > 0) /. x -> -2
#% output
#= undefined

#% cell
1 + conditional_expression(a, false)
#% output
#= undefined

#% text
# A numeric function maps over a list first:

#% cell
gamma([undefined, 2, 5])
#% output
#= [undefined, 1, 24]

#% text
# Connectives and calls of other functions keep it:

#% cell
[undefined or p, f(undefined)]
#% output
#= [undefined or p, f(undefined)]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Drop the undefined entries of a list:

#% cell
select([1, undefined, 3], v => not (v === undefined))
#% output
#= [1, 3]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `conditional_expression`, `piecewise`, `n`
